  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Iowa's federal contract activity in FY2026 to date shows a sharp pullback from recent peaks. Iowa's federal contract obligations are $1.4B. Award activity through the fiscal year to date includes 18,705 awards and an average award size of $72.3K. Obligations are down 62.5% year over year. Historical context shows higher totals in prior fiscal years: FY25 was $3.6B, FY24 was $3B, FY23 was $3.4B, FY22 was $2.7B, and FY21 was $2.5B. The Department of Defense accounts for the largest share of current-year obligations with $866M. Other significant buying agencies include the Department of the Treasury with $175M and the Department of Agriculture with $104M. Other major vendors in the state include ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. at $309M and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC at $254M. Other large industry concentrations in FY2026 to date include Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $263M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $116M. These figures are partial totals for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Iowa's FY2026 to date obligations are $1.4B, lower than the prior five fiscal years. FY25 obligations were $3.6B and FY24 obligations were $3B, with FY23 at $3.4B, FY22 at $2.7B, and FY21 at $2.5B. Obligations are down 62.5% year over year, reflecting a meaningful reduction in current-year spending versus the recent peak. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $72.3K across 18,705 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors are the biggest players in Iowa federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency in FY2026 to date with $866M in obligations, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $175M and the Department of Agriculture with $104M. ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. is the largest vendor with $309M, followed by DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC with $254M and PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. with $116M. Industry concentrations include Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $263M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $116M. These buyers, vendors, and industries represent the bulk of FY2026 to date activity in Iowa."
      }
    ]
  },
